<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-SBC Warburg cuts oil sector stocks.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-SBC Warburg cuts oil sector stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Petroleum and Shell Transport and Trading led the oil sector lower on Thursday as SBC Warburg downgraded the sector.</p>
<p>Shares in British Petroleum were off 7p at 681p by 0908 GMT, after the ADRs fell $2.25 to $130.375 in New York.</p>
<p>Shell, meanwhile, fell 5-1/2p to 10.51-1/2 stg despite the resurgence of bid rumours.</p>
<p>&quot;We are underweight on the sector for the first time since 1993,&quot; SBC Warburg confirmed, commenting that the integrated stocks had been cut from &quot;neutral&quot; and independent's were switched from a previously &quot;overweight&quot; position.</p>
</text>
